2025-08-02 20:17:45,197 [INFO] models.read_document - Read PDF file form web adobe-compendium.md 2025-07-21
1 / 2Selection Process (Adobe):
1. Online Aptitude T est (Duration: 1.5 hrs.):
First, there was an online round of 1 hr. 30 min. 1hr was for aptitude which consisted of 60 questions based on
mental ability, OOPS, probability, reasoning and next 30 min was for 2 coding questions that were of easy
level. Coding questions were easy so overall shortlisting was done based on aptitude. Shortlisted candidates
were called for interviews.
2. Interview (Duration: 45 mins):
We had only a single round and I was asked questions based on my projects, DSA, OOPS, CN and puzzles.
Question 1. What is the difference between SQL and NoSQL database?
Question 2. Why did you choose MongoDB for your project and not other databases?
Question 3. What happens when you type something in search bar of google and hit enter?
Question 4. Given an array of positive integers and you have to multiply all the elements and print the answer
but the time complexity should be less than O(n).
Question 5. What is the difference between compile-time and run-time polymorphism?
Question 6. Given N teams and you have to organise a knockout football tournament. What will be the
number of matches that will be played in the entire tournament?
Question 7. Y ou have 10 boxes of balls (each ball weighing exactly 10 gm) with one box with defective balls
(each one of the defective balls weigh 9 gm). Y ou are given an electronic weighing machine and only one
chance at it. How will you find out which box has the defective balls?
Question 8. Given an array of lowercase English alphabet letters and you have to print the elements
lexicographically. T ry to optimise your approach.
Question 9. Given are N ropes of different lengths, the task is to connect these ropes into one rope with
minimum cost, such that the cost to connect two ropes is equal to the multiplication of their lengths.
Question 10. A binary tree and a number k are given. Print every path in the tree with sum of the nodes in the
path as k. A path can start from any node and end at any node. They need not be root node and leaf node;
and negative numbers can also be there in the tree.
Question 11. Given a binary tree and two node values, your task is to find the minimum distance between
them. The given two nodes are guaranteed to be in the binary tree and nodes are numbered from 1 to N.
Please note that the given two nodes are not always leaf nodes.
Tips for juniors:
1. Do your utmost to keep CPI over 8 because it will help you a lot in becoming eligible for all companies
that will be opened for mechanical.
2. Try to make 2–3 projects for CV as it makes a good impression and questions from projects are
comparatively easier as only standard questions are asked.
adobe-compendium.md 2025-07-21
2 / 23. Try to give at least one contest every week and practice as much DSA as you can.
4. Be patient while explaining your approach, don’t get excited if you already know the solution. T ry to
begin with naïve approach and slowly proceed to your most optimized solution. This will definitely
impress the interviewer.
5. In my opinion PORs and extracurriculars are not that much important.
6. Try to be confident during interviews and practice mock interviews with your friends. I wish you good
luck for internship season.

