latter is used by more than one billion people. These essential  document tools, as well  as powerful mobile 
apps, make up the Adobe Document Cloud, a modern way to manage critical documents at home, in the 
office and across devices, extending a l egacy that began more than 25 years ago.  
As a Product Management Intern, you will work on some of the valuable, exciting customer problems 
across Adobe’s cloud businesses spanning Content, Data and Artificial Intelligence.  Product Management Intern 
Product Management Intern  Page 2 of 2 What you will do  
• Conduct primary and secondary research to identify user needs and emerging trends
• Understand competitor and partner landscape and generate meaningf ul insights
• Pitch and validate new product ideas for internal and external partners
• Contribute to Product, Go to Market vision and strategy
• Build requirement documents and specs, detailing out user journey and use cases.
• Collaborate with Design and Engineering teams to create proof of concept, actual implementation
What you will need  
•Current first year MBA student with outstanding academic record and 
graduating in year 2026
•Strong communication and interpersonal  skills
•Passion for technology
•Aptitude and motivation for a product management role
•Ability to manage ambiguity
•Strong analytical,  problem solving and data management skills
•Customer centricity and focus on user experience
•Prior technical  and relevant experience would be a plus
•Available to do a full-time internship for 10 weeks starti ng April or May 2025
What yo u will gain 
• Mentoring and guidance from an experienced Adobe employee
• Opportunities to be creative, be a leader and be focused
• Wellbeing resources
• Professional learning and development
• A market competitive stipend
At
 Adobe, you will be immersed in an exceptional work environment that is recognized throughout the 
world on  Best Companies lists. You will also be surrounded by colleagues who are committed to helping 
each other grow through our unique  Check -In approach  where ongoing feedback flows freely.   
If you’re looking to make an impact, Adobe's the place for you. Discover what our employees are saying 
about their career experiences on the Adobe Life blog  and explore the meaningful  benefits  we offer.  
Adobe is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome and encourage diversity in the workplace regardless of gender, race or color, ethnicity or national origin, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or veteran status.   

